<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Upper Yafa Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Mahjaba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A loose sultanate of the upper Yafa highlands, one of the most independent of the British protectorate states of south Arabia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Like its neighbour the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lower-yafa-sultanate">Lower Yafa Sultanate</a>, Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a> emerged in the early 18th century when the Yafa tribes rejected rule by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qasimid-state">Qasimid State</a>. The sultans of the Harhara family, based at Mahjaba, held a loose primacy over the upper Yafa clans and their sheikhdoms.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Authority was weak and shared with several sheikhs, and the sultanate had almost no administration. Its rugged highlands were famous for their stone tower houses and terraces, and many of its men emigrated or served as soldiers in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Hadramawt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a> entered British protection late and stayed outside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a>, remaining part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Aden Protectorate</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1967, as British rule ended, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took control and Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a> was incorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/upper-yafa-sultanate.jpg" alt="Upper Yafa Sultanate" width="320" height="193"><figcaption>Image: Xwejnusgozo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Upper_Yafa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mahjaba</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Upper Yafa, Sultanate of Upper Yafa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=upper-yafa-sultanate" aria-label="Upper Yafa Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5920 1663 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Upper Yafa Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6240 1919L6295 1853M6240 1919L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6240 1919h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6240 1919h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=upper-yafa-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
